{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790285454,"nonce":"4uDVWzI+P7Vqo6c/lXT4phabHHI=","title":"A hot reload drops host registrations, and Type.resolveClass cannot see a host-only class","message":"Split out of 3be8b0b.\n\n- `apply_pending_reload` re-decodes the program from disk, so every\n  `register_host_module` a host made against the first decode is gone from\n  the reloaded `DecodedBytecode`: its appended types, natives, globals and\n  `host_natives`. A reload needs to replay the registrations (the host's\n  `HostModule` values, kept alongside the program) before the diff.\n- `Type.resolveClass(\"host.X\")` for a class the host appended (not one it\n  bound, see 3be8b0b) finds nothing: resolution walks the program's\n  declared class names, and an appended class is not among them.","files":null}]}